{
  "$comment": "The Feature Library's single source of truth, read by the website (app/models/finance/module_catalog.rb) and the apps (packages/shared-types/src/modules.ts). Names and descriptions are translation keys (config/locales/billie_modules.*.yml, clients/universal/src/i18n/modules.ts). Availability is per surface: 'web' is the Rails website; 'app' is the universal client (clients/universal) on macOS, Windows, iOS and Android. A module is 'available' on a surface only when its essential journey works there; otherwise 'coming_soon' (shown, never enabled). Hiding a module never changes or deletes data, and never stops processing (e.g. recurring entries still post). Settings is a system entry, not a module, and cannot be hidden.",
